<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description> (255-char cap), and it is INSIDE
        the root element on purpose - a comment ABOVE <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at
        conversion with the misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file".

        THE CANONICAL RATIONALE IS ON THE LEAD TWIN, objects/Lead/fields/Listing_Status__c.
        Read it there: why the picklist is restricted, why blank is permitted, why there is
        no <default>, and the Broker_Listing__c.Listing_Status__c name collision (a
        completely different value set on the disposition side - nothing may ever map
        between them). It is recorded once, deliberately, so the two cannot drift.

        WHY THIS FIELD IS ON OPPORTUNITY AND NOT ON Property__c. LeadConvertService splits
        the extracted field set BY MEANING (ARCHITECTURE.md sec 2, Conversion Enrichment
        S1/S2): deal-process facts go to the Opportunity, physical property facts go to
        Property__c. Whether a seller is marketing publicly or shopping privately is a fact
        about the SALE PROCESS, not about the building - it changes when the seller changes
        strategy while the building does not. It therefore sits beside Sale_Process__c,
        Offer_Due_Date__c and the listing-broker fields, all of which took the same route.

        THE WRITE IS DESCRIBE-GUARDED AT CONVERSION AND MUST STAY THAT WAY. This is a
        RESTRICTED picklist, and LeadConvertService's update is all-or-none - so one
        off-list value would roll back the whole update and take the structural
        RecordTypeId / Property__c link with it. That guard is an existing rule in that
        class, not a new requirement of this field.
    -->
    <fullName>Listing_Status__c</fullName>
    <description>Whether the seller is marketing this property publicly (On Market) or shopping it privately (Off Market). Carried from Lead.Listing_Status__c at conversion. Unrelated to Broker_Listing__c.Listing_Status__c - never map between them.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>On Market = publicly marketed. Off Market = privately shopped. Carried from the Lead at conversion; blank when the email did not say.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Listing Status</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Picklist</type>
    <valueSet>
        <restricted>true</restricted>
        <valueSetDefinition>
            <sorted>false</sorted>
            <value>
                <fullName>On Market</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>On Market</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Off Market</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Off Market</label>
            </value>
        </valueSetDefinition>
    </valueSet>
</CustomField>
